# What must never reach a build context.
#
# `node_modules` is the one that matters. Every Dockerfile here installs dependencies
# from the lockfile and *then* copies sources; without this file that copy drops the
# host's `node_modules` on top of the one just installed. On Windows those are
# junctions into the host pnpm store, so they resolve to nothing inside the image and
# the build fails with "Cannot find module .../typescript/bin/tsc". On Linux they
# resolve to the wrong thing, which is worse — it builds, with whatever the developer
# happened to have.
#
# It is also most of the build context by size, so this is the difference between a
# second and a minute before anything starts.

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output. Every image builds its own from source.
dist
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo

# Not ignored on purpose: apps/lite-action/dist is committed (CLAUDE.md rule 4), but no
# image builds the Action, so the pattern above costs nothing.

.git
.github
.vscode
.idea

# Local environment and anything that could carry a secret into an image layer.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# Docs, fixtures and screenshots: not needed to run a service.
docs
*.md
!apps/*/README.md

# Test and tooling noise.
coverage
.nyc_output
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
